0..78 Comment "// A view: a string held for a block is lent to a view for one access, and the"
79..154 Comment "// view does not own it. The view reads the string it lends, and the access"
155..234 Comment "// ends it exactly once: `resume` writes a string back, `abort` leaves the held"
235..313 Comment "// string as it was and runs the access\'s `unwind` clause. The view lives only"
314..389 Comment "// for its access, so no annotation names how long it lives (the yield-once"
390..463 Comment "// accessor of Hylo\'s subscripts, Racordon and Abrahams, \"Borrow checking"
464..541 Comment "// Hylo\", IWACO 2023; boats, \"References are like jumps\"). A view the program"
542..622 Comment "// keeps longer is kept in the region of a scope around it, `at c`, and lives as"
623..702 Comment "// long as that scope: a static extent erased before anything runs (Koronkevich"
703..763 Comment "// and Bowman, _Type Universes as Kripke Worlds_, ICFP 2025,"
764..788 Comment "// doi:10.1145/3747532)."
790..865 Comment "// The lists; the byte lists; the owned bytes; where they live; the writes."
